# Context

## Background
This commit answers review findings on the v0 qualification rules.
The findings: a grouped interval cannot justify a case-level goal,
unreviewed references cannot support a claim, the plan translation
hash was checked too late and per binding only, and revisions lost
the stored runs a later revision needs.

## Why This Way
- The grouped Wilson interval bounds the share of groups with an
  event. With unequal groups, a tiny group-level upper bound can
  hide a large case-level error rate, so the comparison itself is
  unsound. The new incompatible_unit evidence refuses it instead
  of tightening limits.
- Human review is the acceptance gate for references, so it gates
  qualification, not exploration. Provisional labels still measure
  and report why they cannot qualify.
- The translation hash now covers every question check of the plan
  and is checked before any evaluator call, because one changed
  question invalidates all stored assessments.
- replayRuns rides on the revision result so a later revision can
  replay after JSON storage and reload.

